WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.027 --> 00:00:02.550
- Do you know this one?

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.536
(keyboard music)

00:00:05.536 --> 00:00:08.507
They used to say Portland
didn't have good musicians.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:10.145
They would say, "Portland?

00:00:10.145 --> 00:00:11.159
"Where is that?

00:00:11.159 --> 00:00:15.714
"Who do you know in Portland
that's ever done anything?"

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.604
And I say, "I know me (laughing),

00:00:18.604 --> 00:00:20.354
"and I'm having fun."

00:00:21.258 --> 00:00:23.310
(light instrumental music)

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.837
- [Chris] I'm Chris Funk.

00:00:24.837 --> 00:00:27.507
I'm a musician in a band
called The Decemberists,

00:00:27.507 --> 00:00:29.528
and I'm on a journey looking
for the most surprising

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:32.181
and extraordinary people in music.

00:00:32.181 --> 00:00:36.689
My next stop takes me
to the soul of Portland.

00:00:36.689 --> 00:00:39.651
There, I'll meet Ural Thomas,
the Pacific Northwest godfather

00:00:39.651 --> 00:00:41.318
of rhythm and blues.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.908
My town of Portland, Oregon isn't known

00:00:48.908 --> 00:00:52.014
for having a thriving R&amp;B scene.

00:00:52.014 --> 00:00:54.426
But the Portland I know has a secret.

00:00:54.426 --> 00:00:56.421
Hidden in the heart of
the city's music culture

00:00:56.421 --> 00:00:58.931
is a master of soul who
has shared the stage

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:02.589
with the likes of Otis
Redding and James Brown.

00:01:02.589 --> 00:01:06.102
♪ My sunny days stay bright ♪

00:01:06.102 --> 00:01:07.814
This established 78 year old is proving

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:11.045
that great R&amp;B can be found anywhere.

00:01:11.045 --> 00:01:13.304
♪ Everything I do with you baby ♪

00:01:13.304 --> 00:01:14.831
- [Ural] My name is Ural Thomas.

00:01:14.831 --> 00:01:18.206
I'm singing with a band called The Pain.

00:01:18.206 --> 00:01:22.636
We have a very unique
style of rhythm and blues.

00:01:22.636 --> 00:01:26.324
♪ It's all because of you ♪

00:01:26.324 --> 00:01:30.150
♪ Oh, yeah, baby, yeah ♪

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.597
♪ Oh, baby ♪

00:01:32.597 --> 00:01:36.528
I've been an R&amp;B musician
for over 40 years,

00:01:36.528 --> 00:01:39.359
and I've lived in Portland all my life.

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:42.654
(applauding and cheering)

00:01:42.654 --> 00:01:45.737
(light guitar music)

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:47.988
- [Chris] Ural's music has taken him

00:01:47.988 --> 00:01:50.663
as far as the Apollo Theater in Harlem,

00:01:50.663 --> 00:01:52.944
but after experiencing great achievement

00:01:52.944 --> 00:01:56.637
the siren song of Portland
lured him back home.

00:01:56.637 --> 00:01:58.846
- Hey Chris, how ya doin'?

00:01:58.846 --> 00:02:00.169
- [Chris] We met him at his place

00:02:00.169 --> 00:02:02.534
known for its infamous Sunday jam sessions

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:05.287
with some of Portland's best musicians.

00:02:05.287 --> 00:02:08.547
- Portland, to me, is a very positive place.

00:02:08.547 --> 00:02:11.476
So, I come back home where
I know that I'm positive,

00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:14.147
and I figure like, uh, maybe I
can do something in Portland

00:02:14.147 --> 00:02:15.647
to help musicians.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.287
I really have enjoyed sharing my soul.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.316
There are no word shirts
to explain that feeling;

00:02:24.316 --> 00:02:25.649
it's like magic.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.555
- [Chris] Ural has played
music through segregation

00:02:28.555 --> 00:02:30.283
and the Civil Rights Movement,

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:34.450
watching Portland transition
into the city it is today.

00:02:35.511 --> 00:02:39.320
- The Pacific Northwest
was very segregated.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.558
There was a lot of
places that black singers

00:02:41.558 --> 00:02:43.710
and stuff couldn't go.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.316
So then we had opportunity
to show the people

00:02:46.316 --> 00:02:47.732
what music was really about.

00:02:47.732 --> 00:02:50.529
It wasn't about being divided.

00:02:50.529 --> 00:02:52.782
We didn't have no black and white,

00:02:52.782 --> 00:02:55.154
because we all did it together.

00:02:55.154 --> 00:02:58.487
(cheering and clapping)

00:02:59.775 --> 00:03:03.941
I've played with some very
amazing people in my life

00:03:03.941 --> 00:03:07.322
like Mick Jagger, Otis
Redding, Carla Thomas,

00:03:07.322 --> 00:03:09.460
wonderful people.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:12.240
It was a blessing for me
to have all the experiences

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.508
that I can say that I was a part of.

00:03:14.508 --> 00:03:16.461
♪ Don't write to me ♪

00:03:16.461 --> 00:03:18.003
- [Chris] Ural's musical
journey has taken him

00:03:18.003 --> 00:03:19.265
around the country,

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.332
but I'm happy he's made his
way back home to Portland

00:03:21.332 --> 00:03:25.766
because every city needs
an unexpected treasure.

00:03:25.766 --> 00:03:27.989
- I'm back home now with
the most wonderful group

00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:30.405
that I could ever deal with.

00:03:30.405 --> 00:03:33.599
The guys are called The Pain,

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:35.682
and we're gonna bring it.

00:03:37.699 --> 00:03:40.064
(applauding)

00:03:40.064 --> 00:03:40.897
Oh, man.

